===General election===

The treasurer's race pitted [[Thomas Ravenel]], a young millionaire and emerging politician, against [[Grady Patterson]], a nine-term incumbent who did not face primary opposition. The race was largely fought over the state of South Carolina's employee pension fund, with Ravenel taking issue with the state's projected unfunded [[Liability (financial accounting)|liability]] and its failure to invest the fund in [[Stock|equity]] funds, which he claimed would boost returns. Patterson retorted by pointing out Ravenel's inexperience and accusing Ravenel of using the race as a platform to run against incumbent Senator [[Lindsey Graham]], which Ravenel denied was his intention. Ravenel won the election, but was indicted on June 19, 2007 on [[cocaine]] charges and suspended as treasurer.

